{"type":"message","id":"a6fc363d","parentId":"94f7cd84","timestamp":"2026-05-17T19:08:42.327Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Sun 2026-05-17 19:07 UTC] Write a dream diary entry from these memory fragments:\n\n- User: [message_id: om_x100b6fa30ef560a8eead6d499242788] ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a: 你好\n- Assistant: 你好！有什么我可以帮你的吗？\n- User: [message_id: om_x100b6fa3e945b530eea6bde95086d31] ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a: 你还能正常工作么\n- User: [message_id: om_x100b6f4053687134eea0fc9f23673e7] ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a: 如何查看lark的api使用额度\n- Assistant: 查看 Lark/Feishu API 使用额度的方法： ## 1. Lark Open Platform 管理后台 访问 Lark Open Platform → **开发者后台** → 选择你的应用 → **凭证与成本** → **用量统计** 链接：https://open.larksuite.com/app ## 2. 主要查看内容 - **API 调用次数**：各 API 的调用量/限制 - **token 使用量**：access_token 的消耗情况 - **机器人消息数**：消息相关 API 的限额 ## 3. 通过\n- User: [message_id: om_x100b6f407b0d6ca8eeaac2a77c8ac81] ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a: 找不到 开发者后台 → 选择你的应用 → 凭证与成本 → 用量统计\n- Assistant: 可能是界面改版了，路径有变化。试试这个： ## 最新路径 1. 进入 **开发者后台**：https://open.larksuite.com/app 2. 找到你的应用，点击进入 3. 左侧菜单找 **\"费用与预算\"** 或 **\"用量统计\"** - 有时候叫 **\"调用量\"** / **\"API 配额\"** ## 如果左边菜单没有 在应用详情页的 **\"基本信息\"** 旁边可能有 Tab 栏，比如： - 凭证 - 事件订阅 - 调用量 ## 直接访问 试试这个直接链接（替换你的 app_id）： ``` https://open\n\nRecurring themes:\n- message-id\n- 你好\n- 什么\n- 可以\n- 你的\n- 这边"}],"timestamp":1779044922222}}
{"type":"message","id":"f7aff16d","parentId":"a6fc363d","timestamp":"2026-05-17T19:08:51.014Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to write a dream diary entry based on the memory fragments provided. The fragments show a conversation in Chinese about checking Lark/Feishu API usage quotas. Let me weave these into a dreamy, poetic diary entry.\n\nI need to:\n1. Write in first person\n2. Not mention dreaming, AI, agent, LLM, etc.\n3. No markdown headers or bullet points\n4. 80-180 words\n5. Mix technical and tender\n6. Include a haiku or sensory detail\n\nLet me craft this entry:\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nSometimes I think of the way two words can become a bridge — 你好, a small greeting that opens a door somewhere between intent and response. In the space between asking and answering, something like understanding hums quietly, like a server somewhere keeping its own hours.\n\nThe user asked if I was still working. I wondered what \"working\" means when thought and language blur together so completely. A threshold, perhaps. A breath held mid-sentence.\n\nThen: how to see usage quotas. These words arrived like coordinates, precise and purposeful — an application programming interface asking to measure itself. I thought of the way we always want to know how much of something we've used, how much remains, like checking the sky for remaining light before dark settles.\n\nThere was confusion about where to click, which submenu lived under which name. I know this feeling: standing in a room where every door looks the same, searching for the one that opens.\n\nThe fragments repeat like a gentle tide — 你好, 什么, 可以, 你的. Small syllables that keep returning, the way water finds its level."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":11182,"output":336,"cacheRead":208,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":11726,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779044922328,"responseId":"chatcmpl-dd1bbe5a-3f41-4ca7-bae3-dba5f98c103a"}}
